= Hostages in the Senate

The bounty hunter Cad Bane and his gang seize the Senate building and take a group of senators hostage, Caucus members among them. Their price is the release of Ziro the Hutt. After a tense day the Chancellor agrees, the hostages walk free, and the bounty hunters vanish.

How a gang of mercenaries walked into the most guarded building in the galaxy is a question nobody in the Chancellery seems keen to ask. Instead, the Chancellor's allies demand sweeping new security powers.

- @measured: Demand an inquiry, not new powers.
- @crackdown: Back an immediate security crackdown.

@measured
subtitle: −1 political capital. Calms the panic; the Security Act will face a fairer fight.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; fear -= 4; senate_resolve += 0.5; evidence += 0.3

The Caucus demands an inquiry into the Senate Guard's failure. It finds that three security codes were changed the night before, on authority nobody can trace.

@crackdown
subtitle: The Hawks approve; the Security Act will be fast-tracked.
on-arrival: security_fast = 1; hawk_dissent -= 3; pacifist_dissent += 3

The Senate votes for "whatever it takes". The Chancellor's office has a bill ready.
